mCustomer StoriesIntegrationsSupportCustomer supportTrainingGitHub StatusCompanyAboutPartnersChangelogGitHub UniverseGitHub UniverseThe event for developers, by developers — talks, workshops, and what’s next for GitHub.PricingSearch/Sign inSign upAppearance settings\n\n\n\n\n\n      \n        \n  \n          \n    \n\n          You signed in with another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session.\n          You signed out in another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session.\n          You switched accounts on another tab or window. Reload to refresh your session.\n\n      \n    \n\nDismiss alert\n\n\n  \n\n    \n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n\n  \n    \n      \n    \n\n    \n    \n      \n      {{ message }}\n\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n        \n    \n      \n      \n    \n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n  link-assistanthive-mindRepository navigationCodeIssues163 (163)Pull requests187 (187)ActionsProjectsSecurity and qualityInsightsMore items\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n      \n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n  \n  \n  --auto-restart-until-mergeable posts a duplicate '🛑 Automation stopped: the AI session failed' comment after 'Solution Draft Failed' #4087New issueCopy linkNew issueCopy linkOpen#4088Open--auto-restart-until-mergeable posts a duplicate '🛑 Automation stopped: the AI session failed' comment after 'Solution Draft Failed'#4087#4088Copy linkDescriptionkonardopened on Nov 18, 2026Issue body actionsSummary\nWhen an AI session fails with a non-usage-limit error, --auto-restart-until-mergeable posts two comments on the pull request for one failure:\n\n🚨 Solution Draft Failed, which has the error, the models and the uploaded failure log: feat: Add resumable voice fitting and accuracy reports konard/voice-simulator#146 (comment) (2026-11-17T18:26:04Z)\n🛑 Automation stopped: the AI session failed (reason code tool_failure), which repeats the same error two seconds later: feat: Add resumable voice fitting and accuracy reports konard/voice-simulator#146 (comment) (2026-11-17T18:26:06Z)\n\nThe repository owner asked for the second comment to go away (konard/voice-simulator#146 (comment)):\n\nAutomation stopped: the AI session failed was never requirement, so if something failed Solution Draft Failed comment must be enough. --auto-restart-until-mergeable should report nothing if that is complete and total failure\n\nExpected behaviour\nWhen the session fails completely and the Solution Draft Failed comment (with its log) has been posted, --auto-restart-until-mergeable should post nothing more. The failure comment already says that the session ended and links the log.\nActual behaviour\nsrc/solve.auto-merge.lib.mjs (main at c90e4c1): in the if (!toolResult.success) branch (around lines 1064–1094), the loop:\n\nattaches the failure log with attachLogToGitHub(...), which posts 🚨 Solution Draft Failed;\nthen calls reportAutomationStop({ reason: 'tool_failure', mode: 'auto-restart-until-mergeable', ... }), which posts 🛑 Automation stopped: the AI session failed using the tool_failure text in src/automation-stop-reporting.lib.mjs (around line 93).\n\nThe deduplication in reportAutomationStop only compares stop reports with each other. It does not notice that the failure comment for the same session is already on the pull request.\nThe same pattern is at line 1034 for tool_failure_after_resume.\nSuggested fix\n\nIf failLogAttached is true (the Solution Draft Failed comment was posted), skip reportAutomationStop for tool_failure and tool_failure_after_resume. Keep the terminal log line and recordLoopToolFailure.\nPost the stop report only when no failure comment reached the PR (log upload disabled or failed), so that every failure is still reported once.\nAdd a test: a failed session with --attach-logs should give exactly one PR comment.\n\nContext of the failure itself\nThe session failed with Codex emitted error event: Incomplete response returned, reason: max_output_tokens. The last tool activity was at about 16:50Z; a stream reconnect followed at 17:36Z and turn.failed at 18:18:53Z. The failure log is linked from the first comment above. Nothing was lost: every file change the session made had been committed and pushed before it failed (last push: commit 3715ba8). The truncation itself looks like #4079 (the same max_output_tokens ending after a long single Codex turn). This issue is only about the duplicate stop comment.ActivitySign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? Sign in to commentMetadataMetadataAssigneesNo one assignedLabelsNo labelsNo labelsTypeNo typeProjectsNo projectsMilestoneNo milestoneRelationshipsNone yetDevelopmentNo branches or pull requestsIssue actionsOpen in GitHub Copilot app\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n\n\n\n    \n  \n\n  \n\n  \n            \n  Footer\n\n  \n\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n    \n\n\n      \n        &copy; 2026 GitHub,&nbsp;Inc.\n      \n    \n\n    \n      Footer navigation\n\n      \n\n\n          \n            Terms\n          \n\n          \n            Privacy\n          \n\n\n            \n              Security\n            \n\n            \n              Status\n            \n\n          \n            Community\n          \n\n          \n            Docs\n          \n\n          \n            Contact\n          \n\n          \n\n  \n    \n      Manage cookies\n    \n  \n\n\n  \n    \n      \n        Do not share my personal information\n      \n    \n  \n\n      \n    \n  \n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n\n\n  \n    \n    \n\n    \n      \n    \n\n    \n    You can’t perform that action at this time.",
